<header><p class="st-kicker">other · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Domain of Soissons</h1><p class="st-meta">457 CE – 486 CE (approx.) · capital Soissons</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Last Roman-ruled territory in northern Gaul, held by the generals Aegidius and Syagrius until Clovis conquered it in 486.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 457 the emperor Majorian appointed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegidius">Aegidius</a> as commander of the Roman army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>. When Majorian was murdered in 461, Aegidius refused to recognise his successors and kept control of the region between the Somme and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a>, cut off from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegidius">Aegidius</a> ruled as a Roman general rather than a king, allying with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/franks">Franks</a> and fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a> in 463. After his death in 464 his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syagrius">Syagrius</a> held the region from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soissons">Soissons</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gregory-of-tours">Gregory of Tours</a> calls him king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>, though he probably never used the title.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 486 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/salian-franks">Salian Franks</a> defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syagrius">Syagrius</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soissons">Soissons</a>. Syagrius fled to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/visigothic-kingdom">Visigothic Kingdom</a>, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaric-ii">Alaric II</a> handed him over, and Clovis had him killed. The domain became the core of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-franks">Kingdom of the Franks</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/domain-of-soissons.jpg" alt="Domain of Soissons" width="320" height="333"><figcaption>Image: Publius-Vergilius-Maro · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Gaul,_476_AD.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>457 CE – 486 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Soissons</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Aegidius, Syagrius</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Soissons, Roman Domain of Soissons</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=472&amp;focus=domain-of-soissons" aria-label="Domain of Soissons on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4757 456 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Domain of Soissons lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5077 712L5304 942M5077 712L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5077 712h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5077 712h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Soissons. <a href="/atlas?year=472&amp;focus=domain-of-soissons">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
